course: dictionary
lesson: 15320
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Smoothy is a less common spelling of smoothie, and it can mean a cold fruit drink or a charming person who talks in a slick way. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «Mum blended bananas, strawberries and yoghurt to make a cold smoothy for lunch.» The words blended, cold and yoghurt tell you that a smoothy is a drink.
explain: «Tom was such a smoothy that he talked the teacher into moving his seat.» The word talked tells you that a smoothy can also be a person who charms people with clever words. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A smoothy is a thick, cold drink made by blending fruit, often with yoghurt, milk or ice.
fact: Smoothie is the usual spelling of the drink, so smoothy is a less common spelling.
fact: In an informal sense, a smoothy is a person who is charming and confident in a slick way, especially with words.
fact: A smooth-talking smoothy may not always be trusted, so read the whole sentence to see how the word is being used.
exercise: «We drank a cold strawberry smoothy after football.» What is a smoothy in this sentence? | A small fruit tree | A slick talker who charms people | A type of football boot | *A thick cold drink made from blended fruit
exercise: «Ella was such a smoothy that the shopkeeper gave her free sweets.» What does smoothy mean here? | Someone who is tired and sleepy | A cold drink with ice in it | A very tall person | *A charming person who talks in a slick way
exercise: Which spelling is the usual one for the cold fruit drink? | Smoothy | Smoothee | Smoothe | *Smoothie
test: «Blend 2 bananas for every cup of milk to make a smoothy.» How many bananas would you need for 3 cups of milk? | 5 | *6 | 3 | 2
test: «Dad said the salesman was a smoothy, so he did not believe a word.» What does smoothy suggest about the salesman? | *He is charming, but maybe not to be trusted | He is very tired | He is very young | He makes the best fruit drinks
exam: «He was a smoothy, always saying the right thing to win everyone over.» What does smoothy mean in this sentence? | A kind of bicycle | A bus driver | A cold fruit drink | *A charming person who talks in a slick way
